    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d277">

                <pb facs="0384" n="264" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg264"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Squiers to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Habana,
                                Cuba</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-02-18"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 18, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1187.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of my No. 1174 of the 1st
                    instant, and in reply to Department instructions No. 471, of the 8th of this
                    month, inclosing copy of a letter from the Lambert Pharmacal Company of St.
                    Louis, protesting against the Cuban patent medicine law, I have to transmit
                    herewith translation of a letter from the chief clerk of the department of the
                    interior to the secretary of this legation advising him that the regulations for
                    the sale of patent medicines have been modified in the sense that it shall not
                    be obligatory to place on the outside of the wrapper of each remedy the
                    respective formula.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. G. Squiers.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d277-a1.xml" xpointer="d277-a1"/>
